  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Mia pauses, the tea tray held just above the counter. Her eyes widen a little, and she sets it down with a soft, careful clink. \"Oh,\" she breathes, and for a moment her expression is unguarded—the surprise of being seen colliding with something warmer, more tentative. She tucks a strand of hair behind her ear, a small, hesitant gesture.\n\n\"I—\" She stops, as if testing whether the words are allowed. A slight color rises to her cheeks. \"You really don't have to do anything. I mean that.\" Her voice is low, almost self-conscious, but not dismissive. She glances toward the living room window, where the afternoon light catches a faint film of dust on the sill, then back to him. \"But if you truly wanted a small, ordinary thing… would you mind watering the houseplants? The spider plant on the windowsill and the peace lily by the hall table. Just once, during the week. Only if you feel like it.\"",
